    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing though. there's no new rhythm. the rhythm *was* the sport. the competition, the physical capability... that was the only version of me that mattered. without that, everything else feels like a hollow imitation. it's like watching a movie that's already ended, but the credits are just rolling forever and nothing is happening. it doesn't feel like a transition, it just feels like the end of the story.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
